# This .dockerignore uses an "allowlist" approach for security and a minimal build context.
# For more info: https://docs.docker.com/engine/reference/builder/#dockerignore-file
#
# The repo root is the build context for two builds:
#   * .devcontainer/Dockerfile, which copies only the dependency manifests;
#   * voter/Dockerfile, which builds the frontend bundle and the Go backend into
#     one image and therefore needs both frontend/ and voter/ sources.
# room-pass/ still builds from its own narrower context and is unaffected.
#
# Without this file every build would ship external/ (~200MB of vendored
# checkouts) and frontend/node_modules to the daemon.

# 1. Ignore everything by default.
**

# 2. Dependency manifests, used for cache warm-up layers.
!voter/go.mod
!voter/go.sum
!room-pass/go.mod
!room-pass/go.sum
!frontend/package.json
!frontend/package-lock.json

# 3. Sources the voter image actually builds from.
!voter/*.go
!voter/Dockerfile
!frontend/

# 4. Re-exclude what must never enter the frontend build: installed modules and
#    a previous local build. `npm ci` and `npm run build` recreate both, and a
#    host-built dist/ silently shadowing the container build is a nasty way to
#    ship stale assets.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/dist-ssr
